title: Algorithmic construction baseline
tags: ['baseline', 'book']
abstract: >
  Baseline generated by the system builder from infinite families, allowed
  conference masks, and executable finite generators. The only finite-source
  preload is the explicitly marked n=36 exception.
content: |
    from pathlib import Path
    import importlib.util
    import sys

    def _load_baseline_builder():
        system_dir = Path("storage/system").resolve()
        if str(system_dir) not in sys.path:
            sys.path.insert(0, str(system_dir))
        builder_path = system_dir / "build_epoch_book_b_baseline.py"
        spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(
            "epoch_book_b_baseline_builder",
            builder_path,
        )
        module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
        assert spec.loader is not None
        sys.modules[spec.name] = module
        spec.loader.exec_module(module)
        return module

    def solution_batch() -> dict[int, str]:
        builder = _load_baseline_builder()
        witnesses, _manifest, _rejected = builder.build_baseline()
        return witnesses
